"model": "<p><b>(a)</b></p><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>N</th><th>Product</th><th>Times</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>4</td><td>1</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>1</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>2</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>6</td><td>4</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>After the third pass Times = 4 = N, so the loop stops. <b>Result: Product = 6</b> (the algorithm calculates (N − 1)! = 3! = 6).</p><p><b>(b)</b> Pseudocode:</p><pre>START\n   DECLARE Num1, Num2 AS INTEGER\n   PRINT \"Enter two different numbers\"\n   READ Num1, Num2\n   IF Num1 &lt; Num2 THEN\n      PRINT \"The smaller number is \", Num1\n   ELSE\n      PRINT \"The smaller number is \", Num2\n   ENDIF\nSTOP</pre><p>Pascal:</p><pre>program Smaller;\nvar\n  Num1, Num2: integer;\nbegin\n  writeln('Enter two different numbers');\n  readln(Num1, Num2);\n  if Num1 &lt; Num2 then\n    writeln('The smaller number is ', Num1)\n  else\n    writeln('The smaller number is ', Num2);\nend.</pre><p>Python:</p><pre>num1 = int(input(\"Enter the first number: \"))\nnum2 = int(input(\"Enter a different second number: \"))\nif num1 &lt; num2:\n    print(\"The smaller number is\", num1)\nelse:\n    print(\"The smaller number is\", num2)</pre><p>Test: 7 and 3 → prints 3; 2 and 9 → prints 2.</p>",
