"model": "<p><b>(a)</b></p><pre>var\n  MARKS : array[1..10] of integer;</pre><p><b>(b)</b></p><pre>var\n  SUM     : integer;\n  AVERAGE : real;</pre><p><b>(c)</b></p><pre>SUM := 0;</pre><p><b>(d)</b></p><pre>{ I is declared as  I : integer; }\nfor I := 1 to 10 do\n  SUM := SUM + MARKS[I];</pre><p>Complete program (tested: marks 55, 62, 48, 70, 81, 39, 90, 66, 73, 58 give SUM 642 and average 64.20):</p><pre>program AverageMark;\nvar\n  MARKS: array[1..10] of integer;\n  SUM: integer;\n  AVERAGE: real;\n  I: integer;\nbegin\n  for I := 1 to 10 do\n  begin\n    write('Enter mark ', I, ': ');\n    readln(MARKS[I]);\n  end;\n  SUM := 0;\n  for I := 1 to 10 do\n    SUM := SUM + MARKS[I];\n  AVERAGE := SUM / 10;\n  writeln('Average mark = ', AVERAGE:0:2);\nend.</pre><p>Python equivalent:</p><pre>marks = []\nfor i in range(10):\n    marks.append(int(input(f\"Enter mark {i + 1}: \")))\ntotal = 0\nfor m in marks:\n    total = total + m\naverage = total / 10\nprint(\"Average mark =\", round(average, 2))</pre>",
