"model": "<p><b>(a)(i)</b> Mode: <b>batch processing using a print queue (spooling)</b> — jobs are held and printed first in, first out. Reason: ten booths share one printer, so the queue lets every cashier send certificates without waiting, and they print in the order received.</p><p><b>(ii)</b> A <b>range (or consistency) check</b> on the Amount Paid field: the system compares the amount paid with the amount due for that vehicle. If Amount Paid ≥ Amount Due the print command is sent; if it is less, the certificate is not printed and the cashier is alerted.</p><p><b>(b)(i)</b> Linux — Operating system; Intel Core i3-6100U processor — CPU; Quad-HD OLED (2560 × 1440) touchscreen display — Monitor; 4GB RAM — Primary memory; 500GB SATA Hard Drive — Secondary storage device.</p><p><b>(ii)</b> A printer (to print the road tax certificates); also accept keyboard or mouse.</p><p>(c) The payment must update the vehicle licensing database immediately (online/real-time) so that the record shows the vehicle as licensed at once, a second booth cannot accept a duplicate payment, and the receipt is accurate; only the printing can safely wait in the queue.</p><p>(d)</p><pre>START\n   READ RegNo, AmountPaid\n   READ AmountDue FOR RegNo\n   IF AmountPaid &gt;= AmountDue THEN\n      SEND RegNo TO PrintQueue\n   ELSE\n      Shortfall &lt;- AmountDue - AmountPaid\n      PRINT \"Payment short by $\", Shortfall, \". Certificate not printed.\"\n   ENDIF\nSTOP</pre>",
