"model": "<p><b>(a)(i)</b> Barcode reader; Optical mark reader (OMR).</p><p><b>(ii)</b> Barcode reader at a supermarket checkout in Spanish Town: it captures the product code (number) from the barcode on each item, which the system uses to look up the price and update stock. (Or: OMR marking CXC-style multiple-choice answer sheets, capturing the position of pencil marks.)</p><p><b>(b)(i)</b> A turnaround document is a document produced (printed) by a computer, sent out to a person who adds data to it by hand, and then returned and read back into the computer. Example: a GEBE bill payment stub or a multiple-choice answer sheet with candidate details pre-printed.</p><p><b>(ii)</b> When the completed document is returned, it is passed through an OCR or OMR reader, which reads the pre-printed machine-readable data (e.g. account number) and the marks or figures added by the person directly into the computer, so no one has to type the data in.</p><p><b>(c)</b> 16 GB = 16 × 1,024 = 16,384 MB. 16,384 ÷ 5 = 3,276.8, so <b>3,276</b> complete documents fit. (Using 1 GB = 1,000 MB: 16,000 ÷ 5 = 3,200.)</p><p><b>(d)(i)</b> 1. Select (highlight) the paragraph. 2. Click the Review tab ▸ Word Count (or read the word count on the status bar) to see the number of words.</p><p><b>(ii)</b> 1. Select the paragraph (or place the cursor at its start). 2. Click Review ▸ Spelling &amp; Grammar (or press F7). 3. For each flagged word, choose a suggestion and click Change (or Ignore if it is correct) until the check is complete.</p><p><b>(e)(i)</b> Replace lets you look at each occurrence before it is changed, so words that only contain 'print', such as 'printer' and 'printing', are not wrongly turned into 'producer' and 'producing'. Replace All changes every match at once without checking, which could damage the meaning of the paragraph.</p><p><b>(ii)</b> 1. Home ▸ Replace (or Ctrl+H) to open the Find and Replace dialogue box on the Replace tab. 2. In 'Find what' type <b>print</b>, and in 'Replace with' type <b>produce</b> (click More ▸ tick 'Find whole words only' so 'printer' is not changed). 3. Click <b>Replace All</b>, then OK when the count of replacements is shown.</p>",
"key": "<p><b>Mark scheme</b></p><ul><li>(a)(i) Barcode reader (1); OMR (1). (ii) Application (1); data captured (1).</li><li>(b)(i) Produced by computer (1); filled in and returned to be read by computer (1). (ii) Read by OCR/OMR/scanner (1); data entered directly/automatically (1).</li><li>(c) Working (1); 3,276 or 3,276.8 or 3,200 with consistent working (1).</li><li>(d)(i) Select text (1); Review ▸ Word Count / status bar (1). (ii) Select/position (1); Review ▸ Spelling and Grammar / F7 (1); accept/ignore suggestions (1).</li><li>(e)(i) Replace allows each occurrence to be checked (1); avoids unwanted changes e.g. printer/printing (1). (ii) Open Replace (1); enter find/replace words (1); click Replace All (1).</li></ul>",
