"prompt": "<ol type=\"a\"><li>Complete the table below by inserting the MOST appropriate web technology concepts from the following list.<br><b>Web browser &nbsp; Hypertext markup language &nbsp; Hypertext transfer protocol &nbsp; Hyperlink &nbsp; Web server &nbsp; File transfer protocol &nbsp; Uniform resource locator</b><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Web Technology Concept</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td></td><td>Connects webpages to other webpages</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Stores, processes and delivers webpages to client devices on request</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Facilitates communication with client devices for the delivery of webpages</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Software application that allows client devices to access resources and Websites from the Internet</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Text-based application used to create web pages for display on the client devices</td></tr></tbody></table></div><i>(5 marks)</i></li><li>The database tables STUDENTS and SPORTS can be joined in a one-to-many relationship to ensure that data in the two tables remain as accurate as possible.<ol type=\"i\"><li>State the feature that is used to establish and maintain the accuracy of data between the two database tables. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>State why it is necessary to maintain the accuracy of data between the two database tables. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>Outline how the one-to-many relationship is formed between the two database tables. <i>(2 marks)</i></li></ol></li><li>Create a query by completing the following query design view window to extract<ul><li>the fields <b>ID</b>, <b>FirstName</b>, <b>LastName</b> and <b>Phone</b> from the STUDENTS table</li><li>the field <b>SportName</b> from the SPORTS table, for all married students who play football.</li></ul><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"qbe\"><tr><th>Field</th><td>ID</td><td>FirstName</td><td>LastName</td><td>Married</td><td>Phone</td><td>SportNo</td><td>SportName</td></tr><tr><th>Table</th><td>STUDENT</td><td>STUDENT</td><td>STUDENT</td><td>STUDENT</td><td>STUDENT</td><td>SPORTS</td><td>SPORTS</td></tr><tr><th>Sort</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><th>Show</th><td>☐</td><td>☐</td><td>☐</td><td>☐</td><td>☐</td><td>☐</td><td>☐</td></tr><tr><th>Criteria</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><th>or</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table></div><i>(4 marks)</i></li><li>State the record IDs of the record(s) that would be extracted when the query designed in (c) is executed. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li><ol type=\"i\"><li>There are four steps in implementing a program. List THREE of these steps. <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li>Describe what is involved in any TWO of the steps listed in (e) (i). <i>(2 marks)</i></li></ol></li><li>Complete the following pseudocode by writing a nested if-then-else statement to produce the following.<ul><li>If Team A scores more goals than Team B, the algorithm should output Team A is the winner.</li><li>If Team B scores more goals than Team A, then the algorithm should output Team B is the winner.</li><li>Otherwise, the program should output game drawn.</li></ul><pre>START\nWrite \"Enter the name and number of goals scored by Team A\"\nRead Team_A, goals_A\nWrite \"Enter the name and number of goals scored by Team B\"\nRead Team_B, goals_B\n\n\n\nSTOP</pre><i>(5 marks)</i></li></ol><p style=\"text-align:right\"><b>Total 25 marks</b></p>",
