"model": "<p><b>(a)</b></p><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Web Technology Concept</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Hyperlink</td><td>Connects webpages to other webpages</td></tr><tr><td>Web server</td><td>Stores, processes and delivers webpages to client devices on request</td></tr><tr><td>Hypertext transfer protocol (HTTP)</td><td>Facilitates communication with client devices for the delivery of webpages</td></tr><tr><td>Web browser</td><td>Software application that allows client devices to access resources and Websites from the Internet</td></tr><tr><td>Hypertext markup language (HTML)</td><td>Text-based application used to create web pages for display on the client devices</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><b>(b)(i)</b> Referential integrity (enforced on the relationship).</p><p><b>(ii)</b> So that every SportNo stored in STUDENTS matches a real sport in SPORTS — no student can be linked to a sport that does not exist (no orphan records), and a sport cannot be deleted while students are still linked to it.</p><p><b>(iii)</b> SportNo is the primary key in SPORTS and appears as a foreign key in STUDENTS. In the Relationships window, drag SportNo from SPORTS onto SportNo in STUDENTS and tick Enforce Referential Integrity: one sport (one record in SPORTS) can be played by many students.</p><p><b>(c)</b></p><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"qbe\"><tr><th>Field</th><td>ID</td><td>FirstName</td><td>LastName</td><td>Married</td><td>Phone</td><td>SportNo</td><td>SportName</td></tr><tr><th>Table</th><td>STUDENT</td><td>STUDENT</td><td>STUDENT</td><td>STUDENT</td><td>STUDENT</td><td>SPORTS</td><td>SPORTS</td></tr><tr><th>Sort</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><th>Show</th><td>✔</td><td>✔</td><td>✔</td><td>☐</td><td>✔</td><td>☐</td><td>✔</td></tr><tr><th>Criteria</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>Yes</td><td></td><td></td><td>\"Football\"</td></tr><tr><th>or</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table></div><p>(SportNo = \"020\" in the SportNo column is equally correct.)</p><p><b>(d)</b> IDs <b>7</b> (Smith JONES) and <b>14</b> (Brian JOSEPH).</p><p><b>(e)(i)</b> Create (write) the source code; translate/compile the program; link the program; execute (run) the program. (Testing/debugging and maintenance are also accepted.)</p><p><b>(ii)</b> <b>Creating source code:</b> the programmer types the algorithm as instructions in a programming language such as Python or Pascal using an editor. <b>Compiling:</b> a compiler translates the whole source code into machine code (object code), listing any syntax errors to be corrected.</p><p><b>(f)</b></p><pre>START\n   Write \"Enter the name and number of goals scored by Team A\"\n   Read Team_A, goals_A\n   Write \"Enter the name and number of goals scored by Team B\"\n   Read Team_B, goals_B\n   IF goals_A &gt; goals_B THEN\n      Write Team_A, \" is the winner\"\n   ELSE\n      IF goals_B &gt; goals_A THEN\n         Write Team_B, \" is the winner\"\n      ELSE\n         Write \"game drawn\"\n      ENDIF\n   ENDIF\nSTOP</pre><p>Pascal:</p><pre>program Winner;\nvar\n  Team_A, Team_B: string;\n  goals_A, goals_B: integer;\nbegin\n  writeln('Enter the name of Team A'); readln(Team_A);\n  writeln('Enter the goals scored by Team A'); readln(goals_A);\n  writeln('Enter the name of Team B'); readln(Team_B);\n  writeln('Enter the goals scored by Team B'); readln(goals_B);\n  if goals_A &gt; goals_B then\n    writeln(Team_A, ' is the winner')\n  else\n    if goals_B &gt; goals_A then\n      writeln(Team_B, ' is the winner')\n    else\n      writeln('game drawn');\nend.</pre><p>Python:</p><pre>team_a = input(\"Enter the name of Team A: \")\ngoals_a = int(input(\"Goals scored by Team A: \"))\nteam_b = input(\"Enter the name of Team B: \")\ngoals_b = int(input(\"Goals scored by Team B: \"))\nif goals_a &gt; goals_b:\n    print(team_a, \"is the winner\")\nelif goals_b &gt; goals_a:\n    print(team_b, \"is the winner\")\nelse:\n    print(\"game drawn\")</pre><p>Tests: 2–1 → Team A wins; 0–3 → Team B wins; 1–1 → game drawn.</p>",
"key": "<p><b>Mark scheme</b></p><ul><li>(a) 1 each (5).</li><li>(b)(i) Referential integrity (1). (ii) Valid reason (1). (iii) PK in SPORTS (1) linked to FK in STUDENTS (1).</li><li>(c) Show ticked for ID, FirstName, LastName, Phone, SportName (1); Married and SportNo not shown (1); Married criterion Yes/True (1); SportName \"Football\" or SportNo \"020\" on the same row (1).</li><li>(d) 7 (1), 14 (1).</li><li>(e)(i) 1 each for three steps (3). (ii) 1 each for two descriptions (2).</li><li>(f) First IF with correct condition (1); Team A output (1); ELSE with nested IF on goals_B &gt; goals_A (1); Team B output (1); ELSE game drawn with ENDIFs (1).</li></ul>",
