"model": "<p><b>(a)</b></p><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Intranet</th><th>Internet</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td>A private network belonging to one organisation</td><td>A public, global network of networks</td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td>Only authorised employees can access it (log-in required)</td><td>Anyone with a connection can access it</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td>Content is controlled and approved by the organisation</td><td>Content is uncontrolled; anyone can publish</td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td>Smaller, usually faster and more secure (behind a firewall)</td><td>Very large; more exposed to security threats</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><b>(b)</b> Passport number: a <b>format check</b> (or length check) — passport numbers follow a fixed pattern, e.g. one or two letters followed by a set number of digits, so an entry with the wrong pattern or length is rejected. Age: a <b>range check</b> — age must be between sensible limits, e.g. 0 and 120 (or 18 and 100 for an adult form), so negative or impossible ages are rejected.</p><p><b>(c)</b> Term: <b>Phishing</b>. Description for Hacking: gaining unauthorised access to a computer system, network or data, usually by getting round passwords or security controls.</p><p><b>(d)(i)</b> Drag the <b>Salesperson</b> field out of the ROWS area (back to the field list) and drag the <b>Region</b> field into ROWS, leaving Sum of Order Amount in VALUES. The PivotTable then shows East 2150, South 4970, West 3940.</p><p><b>(ii)</b> Leave Salesperson in ROWS and Sum of Order Amount in VALUES, and drag the <b>Month</b> field into the COLUMNS area. Each salesperson's row now has a column for January, February and March, and the Grand Total column gives each salesperson's total.</p><p><b>(iii)</b> <code>=SUM(C2:C16)</code> (= $11,060.00).</p><p><b>(iv)</b> <code>=Quarter1Sales!C17</code></p><p><b>(v)</b> <code>=B2/$C$1*100</code> — the absolute reference $C$1 keeps the total fixed while B2 changes to B3…B7 as it is filled down. (The question says B1, but B1 is the heading; the salesperson's amount starts in B2.) Results: 19.44, 22.15, 29.70, 15.24, 13.47, 100.</p>",
