"model": "<p><b>(a)</b> Benefit: the manager can reach the gallery's files from any device with Internet access (at home or at an art fair), and the files are stored off-site, so they are safe if the notebook is lost, stolen or damaged. Limitation: the files can only be reached with an Internet connection — if the connection is down or slow, the manager cannot open or upload them; also the free plan has limited space and the data is held by a third party, which raises privacy and security concerns.</p><p><b>(b)</b> (i) Biometric fingerprint scanner (reader). (ii) Speakers (a public-address system). (iii) Barcode (or QR-code) scanner/reader. (iv) Keyboard (or touchscreen).</p><p><b>(c)(i)</b> Data is raw, unprocessed facts and figures (e.g. 25, 14/01/2025) with no context, whereas information is data that has been processed and organised so that it has meaning and is useful, e.g. 'Visitors in January 2025: 412'.</p><p><b>(ii)</b></p><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Field Name</th><th>Data Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Customer Name</td><td>Text (short text)</td></tr><tr><td>Date of Visit</td><td>Date/Time</td></tr><tr><td>Ticket Cost</td><td>Currency</td></tr><tr><td>Address</td><td>Text (short text)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><b>(iii)</b> <b>CustomerID</b> (a new field). Reason: each customer gets a unique ID, whereas names and addresses can be shared by different customers, so CustomerID identifies exactly one record.</p><p><b>(iv)</b></p><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>CustomerID</th><th>Customer Name</th><th>Date of Visit</th><th>Ticket Cost</th><th>Address</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>C0001</td><td>Nadia Richardson</td><td>14/01/2025</td><td>$25.00</td><td>12 Broad Street, Bridgetown</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><b>(d)</b> Queries (to search, sort and calculate) and forms (to enter, edit and delete records). Reports present the data.</p>",
