"model": "<p><b>(a)(i)</b> General-purpose software can be used for many different tasks chosen by the user (e.g. a word processor or spreadsheet), whereas special-purpose software is designed to carry out one specific task only (e.g. a payroll program or a GPS navigation app).</p><p><b>(ii)</b> Customized software is an existing off-the-shelf package that is modified or configured by the developer to suit one organisation, e.g. QuickBooks set up with the company's own invoice templates, accounts and macros. Custom-written (bespoke) software is written from scratch specifically for one organisation's needs, e.g. the gallery-management or airline-booking system the programmers in this scenario are building. Customized is cheaper and quicker; custom-written fits exactly but costs more and takes longer.</p><p><b>(b)(i)</b> 1. Check that the printer is switched on, online and connected (USB cable or Wi-Fi) and that it has paper and no paper jam. 2. Check that the correct printer is selected as the default, then open the print queue, clear any stuck job and resend the document (restart the printer/print spooler if necessary).</p><p><b>(ii)</b> 1. Check the ink or toner — replace an empty cartridge (and remove any protective tape from a new one). 2. Run the printer's head-cleaning/nozzle-check utility; also check the document's font colour is not set to white.</p><p><b>(c)</b> Determine the most efficient solution — 3; Develop the algorithm — 4; Propose and evaluate solutions — 2; Test and validate the solution — 5; Define the problem — 1.</p><p><b>(d)</b></p><pre>START\n   DECLARE NumStudents AS INTEGER\n   PRINT \"Enter the number of students in attendance\"\n   READ NumStudents\n   IF NumStudents &lt; 25 THEN\n      PRINT \"contact the school\"\n   ELSE\n      IF NumStudents = 25 THEN\n         PRINT \"all students in attendance\"\n      ELSE\n         PRINT \"trip invoice update required\"\n      ENDIF\n   ENDIF\nSTOP</pre><p>Pascal (tested with 20, 25, 30):</p><pre>program FieldTrip;\nvar\n  NumStudents: integer;\nbegin\n  writeln('Enter the number of students in attendance');\n  readln(NumStudents);\n  if NumStudents &lt; 25 then\n    writeln('contact the school')\n  else if NumStudents = 25 then\n    writeln('all students in attendance')\n  else\n    writeln('trip invoice update required');\nend.</pre><p>Python:</p><pre>num_students = int(input(\"Enter the number of students in attendance: \"))\nif num_students &lt; 25:\n    print(\"contact the school\")\nelif num_students == 25:\n    print(\"all students in attendance\")\nelse:\n    print(\"trip invoice update required\")</pre><p><b>(e)(i)</b> <b>A:</b> 'Print \"Welcome\"' is an output, so it must be drawn in an input/output symbol (parallelogram), not a process rectangle. <b>B:</b> the line looping back from the decision must be labelled <b>No</b> (False) — and, so the loop can end, a process that changes LineNum (e.g. LineNum ← LineNum − 1, or reading LineNum) should be inside the loop. <b>C:</b> the line leaving the decision downwards must be labelled <b>Yes</b> (True) and must end at a <b>Stop</b> terminal (oval); likewise the small circle at the top should be a <b>Start</b> oval.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 320 330\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Corrected flowchart: Start oval, Print Welcome in a parallelogram, process LineNum minus 1, decision LineNum == 0, No loops back, Yes goes to Stop oval\" style=\"max-width:320px;width:100%\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"120.0\" y=\"5.0\" width=\"80\" height=\"26\" rx=\"13.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"21.333333333333332\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\">Start</text><polyline points=\"160,31 160,50\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><polygon points=\"107.0,51.0 237.0,51.0 213.0,81.0 83.0,81.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"69.33333333333333\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\">Print \"Welcome\"</text><polyline points=\"160,81 160,104\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><rect x=\"80.0\" y=\"105.0\" width=\"160\" height=\"30\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"123.33333333333333\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\">LineNum ← LineNum − 1</text><polyline points=\"160,135 160,168\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><polygon points=\"160,169.0 220.0,200 160,231.0 100.0,200\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"197.33333333333334\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\">LineNum</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"209.33333333333334\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\">= = 0 ?</text><polyline points=\"100,200 40,200 40,42 160,42\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7FB2FF\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"192\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-weight=\"bold\">No (B)</text><polyline points=\"160,231 160,290\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#F5C542\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"192\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-weight=\"bold\">Yes (C)</text><rect x=\"120.0\" y=\"291.0\" width=\"80\" height=\"26\" rx=\"13.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"307.3333333333333\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\">Stop</text></svg><figcaption>Corrected flowchart</figcaption></figure><p><b>(ii)</b> Repetition (iteration/loop) — a post-test loop, equivalent to REPEAT … UNTIL LineNum = 0.</p>",
"key": "<p><b>Mark scheme</b></p><ul><li>(a)(i) General (1); special (1). (ii) Customized described (1) + example (1); custom-written described (1) + example (1).</li><li>(b)(i) Any TWO valid actions (2). (ii) Any TWO valid actions (2).</li><li>(c) All five correct = 2; three or four correct = 1 (order: 3, 4, 2, 5, 1).</li><li>(d) START/STOP (1); prompt (1); READ (1); condition &lt; 25 with message (1); condition = 25 with message (1); ELSE &gt; 25 message (1); correct nesting/ELSE IF (1); ENDIF(s) (1).</li><li>(e)(i) A parallelogram (1); B labelled No/False (1); C labelled Yes/True (1); Start/Stop terminals or LineNum update (1). (ii) Loop/repetition/iteration (1).</li></ul>",
"teacherTip": "Current SOs 1.7, 1.10, 7.1, 7.7. In (e) the small circles look like connectors; CXC wanted proper Start/Stop terminals. Many candidates miss that LineNum never changes, so the loop would never end.",
