"prompt": "<ol type=\"a\"><li><ol type=\"i\"><li>State the function which could be used to determine the number of T-shirt types in the spreadsheet document. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>The appearance of a spreadsheet document helps users to understand the data presented. Name THREE numeric formatting features that can be used in a spreadsheet. <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li>Absolute addressing is needed to calculate the <b>Tax cost</b> for each type of T-shirt in the boutique. Explain what the absolute addressing feature means in the following formula. <code>=B12*$B$4</code> <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>Write the formula needed to accurately calculate the <b>Final cost</b> of the <b>Travel</b> T-shirts, if the tax is applied after the discount. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>Write a formula to determine the average <b>Final cost</b> for ALL T-shirts in Vashawn's boutique <b>and</b> state the cell address for the value. <i>(2 marks)</i></li></ol></li><li>All customers entering Vashawn's clothing store can connect to the internet via their mobile devices.<ol type=\"i\"><li>State the name given to the internet access point that allows customers to connect to the Wi-Fi network in the store. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>Describe the function of EACH of the following network technologies used in the store.<ul><li>Network adapter</li><li>Wi-Fi</li><li>Router</li><li>Modem</li></ul><i>(4 marks)</i></li></ol></li><li>Based on the discount percentages for the T-shirts sold at Vashawn's clothing store, where Nature (N) = 10, Slangs (S) = 5, Plain (P) = 2 and Travel (T) = 3, evaluate the following statements and give ONE reason for EACH answer.<ol type=\"i\"><li>T = = (S MOD P = 2) <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li>(S = = P) AND (T &gt; = N) <i>(3 marks)</i></li></ol></li><li>Complete the truth table below.<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>A</th><th>B</th><th>A OR B</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>TRUE</td><td>TRUE</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>TRUE</td><td>FALSE</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>FALSE</td><td>TRUE</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>FALSE</td><td>FALSE</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>State exactly how the following operators are used when representing algorithms in the form of flow charts and pseudocode.<br>Arithmetical operators ……<br>Relational operators …… <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>Write formulas for C12, D12 and E12 that can be copied down to row 15 without editing, and give the four Final costs. Explain why C12 cannot simply be =B12*$B$6. <i>(5 marks)</i></li><li>Evaluate NOT (T &lt; P) OR (N MOD S = 0) and give a reason. <i>(2 marks)</i></li></ol><p style=\"text-align:right\"><b>Total 32 marks</b></p>",
