"model": "<p><b>(a)(i)</b> Track Changes. <b>(ii)</b> 'All Markup' (Final Showing Markup) — shows the new text with deletions struck through; and 'No Markup' (Final) — shows only the updated text (also Simple Markup or Original).</p><p><b>(b)</b> Document formatting: centre alignment of the headings and table; a border around the page (the notice is boxed) — also shading in the table heading row and an inserted graphic. Character formatting: bold and underline (heading); superscript (4<sup>th</sup>, footnote number ¹); italics (pie-chart title); strikethrough (track-changes deletions).</p><p><b>(c)</b> Microsoft Excel (spreadsheet) and Microsoft PowerPoint (or Access).</p><p><b>(d)</b> 1. In the other open application, select the graphic and click Copy (Ctrl+C). 2. Switch to the notice, click at the place where the graphic should go and click Paste (Ctrl+V), then size and position it (wrap text as needed).</p><p><b>(e)</b> Columns: 2. Rows: 4 (including the heading row).</p><p><b>(f)</b></p><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Text</th><th>Name of Feature</th><th>Purpose of Feature</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The heading 'Number of Reports' in the table</td><td>Cell shading (with bold and text wrapping)</td><td>Makes the heading row stand out from the data and keeps the long heading within the column width</td></tr><tr><td>The statement at the bottom of the notice</td><td>Footnote</td><td>Gives extra explanation (the times when reports end) without cluttering the main text; linked by the superscript number 1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><b>(g)</b> Name of function: Find and Replace (Replace All). Result: every occurrence of 'REPORT' in the document is changed to 'REPORTED' in one action; unless 'Find whole words only' is ticked, words that contain REPORT are also changed, e.g. 'Reports' becomes 'REPORTEDs', so the result should be checked.</p>",
"key": "<p><b>Mark scheme</b></p><ul><li>(a)(i) Track changes (1). (ii) 1 each for two views (2).</li><li>(b) 1 each: two document features, two character features (4).</li><li>(c) 1 each (2).</li><li>(d) Copy from source (1); paste at location (1). Accept Insert ▸ Object/Picture.</li><li>(e) 2 columns (1); 4 rows (1).</li><li>(f) Feature (1) + purpose (1) for each (4). Heading: accept shading, text wrap, bold, centre.</li><li>(g) Find and Replace / Replace All (1); all occurrences changed (1); note on partial words or case (1).</li></ul>",
