"prompt": "<ol type=\"a\"><li>Management has been trying to reduce the source of virus attacks at a company. Match each of the following statements with the appropriate step in the table below. Write the corresponding letter in the space provided. Each statement can be used more than once.<br><b>Statements:</b> A. No viruses found after scanning &nbsp; B. Scan computer files and documents for new viruses &nbsp; C. Computers are infected with viruses &nbsp; D. Install antivirus software<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Steps</th><th>Corresponding Letter of Statement</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>I. Definition of the problem</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>II. Propose a solution</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>III. Select most efficient solution</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>IV. Test the solution</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>V. Validate the solution</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><i>(4 marks)</i></li><li>Identify the generation and level of programming language in EACH of the following examples.<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Example</th><th>Generation</th><th>Level</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>(i) A user opens a file by clicking on an icon</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>(ii) The computer interprets a password as 0011010100011001010100100</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>(iii) An encoded file is stored as a series of digits and letters which look as 7F 2A 12</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>(iv) A programmer wrote an antivirus program using code such as SELECT user FROM Dept WHERE Virus_scan &gt; 7</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>(v) A virus is written using code such as: LDA 32 / ADD #2 / STA B / JMP #5</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>(vi) A fingerprint is used as a password for a laptop</td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><i>(12 marks)</i></li><li>Study the flowchart in the stimulus and answer the questions that follow.<ol type=\"i\"><li>State whether the flowchart contains EACH of the following.<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Symbols</th><th>Yes or No</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Start/Stop</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Input/Output</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Process</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Decision</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Directional arrow</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><i>(5 marks)</i></li><li>State whether the flowchart illustrates the characteristics of an algorithm. Give a reason for your answer. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>Complete the following trace table using statements from the flowchart.<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Virus Definitions and Security Patches Updated?</th><th>Files being Downloaded without being Scanned First?</th><th>Results</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Y</td><td>Y</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Y</td><td>N</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>N</td><td>Y</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>N</td><td>N</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><i>(4 marks)</i></li><li>Write a fragment of pseudocode starting from the symbol numbered 2 in the flowchart. <i>(3 marks)</i></li></ol></li></ol><p style=\"text-align:right\"><b>Total 30 marks</b></p>",
