"model": "<p><b>(a)</b> I Definition of the problem — <b>C</b> (computers are infected). II Propose a solution — <b>D</b> (install antivirus software; B also accepted). III Select most efficient solution — <b>D</b>. IV Test the solution — <b>B</b> (scan files for new viruses). V Validate the solution — <b>A</b> (no viruses found after scanning).</p><p><b>(b)</b></p><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Example</th><th>Generation</th><th>Level</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>(i) Clicking an icon</td><td>5th (visual/GUI, natural interaction)</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>(ii) 0011010100011001010100100</td><td>1st (machine code)</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>(iii) 7F 2A 12 (hexadecimal machine code)</td><td>1st</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>(iv) SELECT user FROM Dept WHERE …</td><td>4th (SQL query language)</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>(v) LDA 32 / ADD #2 / STA B / JMP #5</td><td>2nd (assembly language)</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>(vi) Fingerprint as a password</td><td>5th (natural, biometric input; no code written by the user)</td><td>High</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Notes: machine code in binary or in hexadecimal shorthand is still first-generation; LDA/ADD/STA/JMP are assembly mnemonics (second generation); SELECT…FROM…WHERE is SQL, a fourth-generation (non-procedural) language. Both 1GL and 2GL are low-level; 3GL and above are high-level.</p><p><b>(c)(i)</b> Start/Stop — Yes (only a STOP terminal is shown). Input/Output — No. Process — Yes. Decision — Yes. Directional arrow — Yes.</p><p><b>(ii)</b> Yes. It has a finite number of clear, unambiguous steps that are carried out in a logical order (sequence, selection and a loop back to re-check), and every path ends at STOP, so it terminates. (Answer 'No' with the reason 'it has no START and no input/output' was also creditable.)</p><p><b>(iii)</b></p><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Updated?</th><th>Downloaded without being scanned?</th><th>Results</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Y</td><td>Y</td><td>Activate mandatory file scanning</td></tr><tr><td>Y</td><td>N</td><td>Check for other issues</td></tr><tr><td>N</td><td>Y</td><td>Update antivirus software (then check again)</td></tr><tr><td>N</td><td>N</td><td>Update antivirus software (then check again)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><b>(iv)</b></p><pre>IF Files being downloaded without being scanned first = \"Y\" THEN\n   Activate mandatory file scanning\nELSE\n   Check for other issues\nENDIF\nSTOP</pre><p>Whole flowchart as a Pascal program (tested: N, Y, Y → update, then 'Activate mandatory file scanning'):</p><pre>program VirusCheck;\nvar\n  Updated, Unscanned: char;\nbegin\n  writeln('Virus definitions and security patches updated? (Y/N)');\n  readln(Updated);\n  while Updated &lt;&gt; 'Y' do\n  begin\n    writeln('Update antivirus software');\n    writeln('Virus definitions and security patches updated? (Y/N)');\n    readln(Updated);\n  end;\n  writeln('Files being downloaded without being scanned first? (Y/N)');\n  readln(Unscanned);\n  if Unscanned = 'Y' then\n    writeln('Activate mandatory file scanning')\n  else\n    writeln('Check for other issues');\n  writeln('STOP');\nend.</pre>",
