"model": "<p><b>(a)</b> A flowchart.</p><p><b>(b)</b> (i) Input: 2. (ii) Process: 1 (also 5 or 6). (iii) Output: 7. (iv) A condition: 3 (or 4).</p><p><b>(c)</b> Symbol 3: the box on the branch to symbol 7 (left) = <b>Y</b>; the box on the branch down to symbol 4 = <b>N</b>. Symbol 4: the box on the branch to symbol 6 (left) = <b>N</b>; the box on the branch down to symbol 5 = <b>Y</b>.</p><p><b>(d)</b></p><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Day</th><th>Sequence of Symbols Used</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sunday</td><td>1, 2, 3, 4, 6 (then back to 2)</td></tr><tr><td>Tuesday</td><td>1, 2, 3, 4, 5 (then back to 2)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>(For a second or later day, symbol 1 is not repeated: 2, 3, 4, 6 and 2, 3, 4, 5.)</p><p><b>(e)</b></p><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Symbol</th><th>Value or Operator</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A constant</td><td>1</td><td>0 (or symbol 3: 7)</td></tr><tr><td>A relational operator</td><td>3</td><td>&gt;</td></tr><tr><td>An arithmetic operator</td><td>3</td><td>+ (or symbol 5/6: add 1, i.e. +)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><b>(f)</b> <code>Weekday := Weekday + 1;</code></p><p><b>(g)</b> It initialises the two counters, Weekday and Weekend, to zero before any days are counted.</p><p><b>(h)</b></p><pre>if (Day &lt;&gt; 'Saturday') and (Day &lt;&gt; 'Sunday') then\n  Weekday := Weekday + 1\nelse\n  Weekend := Weekend + 1;</pre><p>(No semicolon before <code>else</code> in Pascal.)</p><p><b>(i)</b> The program accepts days one at a time and counts how many are weekdays and how many are weekend days (Saturday/Sunday); when more than 7 days have been counted it prints the number of weekdays and the number of weekend days.</p><p>Complete program (a REPEAT loop with &gt;= 7 so exactly one week is counted; tested with Monday–Sunday → Weekdays 5, Weekend days 2):</p><pre>program CountDays;\nvar\n  Day: string;\n  Weekday, Weekend: integer;\nbegin\n  Weekday := 0;\n  Weekend := 0;\n  repeat\n    write('Enter a day: ');\n    readln(Day);\n    if (Day &lt;&gt; 'Saturday') and (Day &lt;&gt; 'Sunday') then\n      Weekday := Weekday + 1\n    else\n      Weekend := Weekend + 1;\n  until Weekday + Weekend &gt;= 7;\n  writeln('Weekdays: ', Weekday);\n  writeln('Weekend days: ', Weekend);\nend.</pre><p>Python:</p><pre>weekday = 0\nweekend = 0\nwhile weekday + weekend &lt; 7:\n    day = input(\"Enter a day: \")\n    if day not in (\"Saturday\", \"Sunday\"):\n        weekday += 1\n    else:\n        weekend += 1\nprint(\"Weekdays:\", weekday)\nprint(\"Weekend days:\", weekend)</pre>",
"key": "<p><b>Mark scheme</b></p><ul><li>(a) Flowchart (1).</li><li>(b) 1 each (4).</li><li>(c) 1 per box (4).</li><li>(d) 2 per correct sequence (4); 1 if one symbol is missing.</li><li>(e) Symbol (1) + value/operator (1) for each item (6).</li><li>(f) Weekday (1) := (1) Weekday + 1 (1) ; (1).</li><li>(g) Initialise counters to zero (1).</li><li>(h) if with condition (1); then Weekday := Weekday + 1 (1); else (1); Weekend := Weekend + 1; (1).</li><li>(i) Counts weekdays and weekend days (1); prints the counts after 7+ days (1).</li></ul>",
"teacherTip": "Previous-syllabus 032, but flowcharts, Pascal assignment and IF-THEN-ELSE are current SOs 7.7 and 8.1. Grade One point: 'Weekday + Weekend &gt; 7' is only checked BEFORE a day is processed, so 8 days are counted before printing — an off-by-one error; '&gt;= 7' (or = 7) counts exactly one week. There is also no START or STOP symbol.",
